  "body": {
    "givenName": "CryptoRich (CRICH)",
    "image": {
      "@type": "ImageObject",
      "contentUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CryptoRichBlog/p/main/logo.png",
      "sha256": "93e5750945d0dcce9b325ed78407558c84f8ffefdf4366ea178828e437ab45bc"
    },
    "motivations": "I run the CRICH stake pool and delegate my own ADA to it. Many Korean holders keep their ADA on exchanges and have little voice in governance. I want to give them a DRep who explains each decision in their language, and to treat the treasury the way a careful business treats its own budget.",
    "objectives": "Read every governance action in full and vote on each one before it expires. Publish the reasoning for every vote in English and Korean on crich.io, X and the CryptoRich blog. Judge treasury withdrawals by who pays, who benefits, and whether milestones measure real use rather than activity.",
    "qualifications": "Career in digital-asset strategy in finance. Operator of the CRICH stake pool on Cardano mainnet since October 2026. Author of the CryptoRich blog, which covers Cardano staking and governance for Korean readers.",
